{"name":"Manila Tint","hex":"#ffe2a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"manila","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of manila paper or material like it.","Yellow-brown; colored like manila paper."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Fiber made from abaca (Manila hemp), used to make ropes and manila paper.","The yellow-brown color of manila."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/manila"},{"term":"tint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slight coloring.","A pale or faint tinge of any color; especially, a variation of a color obtained by adding white (contrast shade)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shade, to color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tint"}],"entries":[{"title":"Manila","blocks":[{"text":"Manila, officially the City of Manila, is the capital and second-most populous city of the Philippines after Quezon City. According to the 2024 census, it has a population of 1,902,590 people. Located on the eastern shore of Manila Bay on the island of Luzon, it is classified as a highly urbanized city. With 44,935 inhabitants per square kilometer (116,380/sq mi), Manila is one of the world's most densely populated cities proper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Cityscape_of_Manila%2C_2025_%2801%29.jpg/330px-Cityscape_of_Manila%2C_2025_%2801%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manila","wikidata":"Q1461"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone","wikidata":"Q2749750"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/500px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/1280px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Rizal_Monument.jpg/500px-Rizal_Monument.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARizal_Monument.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg/500px-Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg/1280px-Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg/500px-Gate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_%2835201250583%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGate_of_Fort_Santiago_-_38923-Manila_(35201250583).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/San_Agustin_Church%2C_Intramuros%2C_Manila_City.jpg/500px-San_Agustin_Church%2C_Intramuros%2C_Manila_City.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wiki